F003 (rubin-prims-dsa): FlashInfer Prims-TS sparse MLA on SM107, a backport of
flashinfer-ai/flashinfer#8186 (commit 784bfaf5bda80259d11a41955ab8c979914197f1, merged on main
2026-11-02, in no release yet), restricted to flashinfer/attention/prims_ts/**/*.py
(upstream README and test hunks dropped). Applies with -p1 on top of F001 (FlashInfer main
26bb6dc93 prims_ts vendored onto the image's flashinfer-python 0.7.2), i.e. inside
/opt/sglang/lib/python3.12/site-packages. Pure CuTe DSL Python: no csrc, no AOT/jit-cache change;
the kernels JIT-compile at first plan for the device's own target (sm_107a with
nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.8.0, the image's).
  - mla_decode.py: sparse MLA planning uses the shared _validate_runtime_device check
    (SM100/SM103/SM107, plus require_cute_dsl_arch on SM107) instead of SM100/SM103 only.
  - helpers/nvfp4_kv.py, throughput_2cta/nvfp4_kv_load.py: SM107 NVFP4 KV converter (SM107's
    ptxas rejects the packed mul.e4m3x4.e2m1x4). NVFP4 KV only; the native-FP8 path SGLang's
    flashinfer_prims_ts uses is unchanged.
Regenerate: git -C flashinfer show --format= 784bfaf5 -- 'flashinfer/attention/prims_ts/*.py'

